 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for change delivery.** Committed revisions are pushed over self-hosted WebSockets rather than five-second HTTPS polling or a hosted realtime service. Polling was rejected because it adds repeated read load and multi-second lag; a hosted realtime service was rejected to avoid recurring realtime vendor fees and provider coupling. This accepts the operational responsibility of connection capacity, session management, replayable revision storage, and browser reconnect catch-up. See `docs/decisions/change-delivery.md`.
